---
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.about;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<DocumentLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <ContentCard>
<p class="section-kicker">TENSOR Standards Consortium</p>
    <h2>Purpose and scope</h2>
    <p>TENSOR is a public standard initiative for cyber investigations. Its shared model represents questions, evidence references, assessments, decisions, and revisions so an investigation can be understood and continued across people, agents, organizations, and tools.</p>
    <p>The scope includes incident response, threat hunting, digital forensics, identity, host, network, cloud, email, application, file, and AI-system investigations.</p>
    <h2>Public foundation, specialized implementations</h2>
    <p>The public Core defines the investigation model. Public graphs and profiles supply shared technical questions and evidence criteria. Vendor and organization graphs add product knowledge, local policy, integrations, and operational workflow.</p>
    <p>The shared model is independent of a particular interface, model provider, storage system, or execution engine. <a href="/extensions/">The layering guide</a> describes these responsibilities and includes a working example.</p>
    <h2>Available resources</h2>
    <ul><li><a href="/core/">Core 0.1.0-draft.1</a>: logical contract, JSON binding, schemas, and reference validator.</li><li><a href="/graphs/">Investigation atlas</a>: 609 current public questions across seven domains. Earlier releases remain in the historical archive.</li><li><a href="/graphs/profiles/">Event profiles</a>: sixteen draft event contexts and example investigation paths.</li><li><a href="/investigation-lab/">Investigation Lab</a>: local record inspection, validation, replay, and exchange.</li><li><a href="/studio/">Graph Studio</a>: graph and layer import, combination, and export.</li></ul>
    <h2>Project status</h2>
    <p>Core is an unratified implementation candidate. John Schieferle Uhlenbrock is the bootstrap steward, convenor, Core editor, and conformance maintainer under the TENSOR Standards Consortium project identity. The broader governance proposal, external review, and independent interoperability evidence remain open.</p>
    <p><a href="/governance/">Stewardship and governance</a> · <a href="/review/">Technical review package</a> · <a href="/read/founding/00-charter/">Founding charter</a> · <a href="/docs/">Resource directory</a></p>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
